  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-42153",
      "knowledge_point_id": "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination",
      "problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )",
              "option": "0",
